    {
      "id": "lEQa",
      "code_hash": "8155c69eb0eca677d64db800951c8899",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"1-start-from-the-general-static-spherically-symmetric-ansatz-eq-241\">1) Start from the general static, spherically symmetric ansatz (Eq. 24.1)</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The notes begin with</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nds^2 = -A(r)dt^2 + B(r)dr^2 + 2C(r)dr\\,dt + D(r)r^2(d\\theta^2 + \\sin^2\\theta\\,d\\phi^2).\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">Then they simplify this ansatz by coordinate redefinitions:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>remove the cross-term via a new time coordinate (Eqs. 24.2-24.4), so <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(C(r)=0||)</marimo-tex></li>\n<li>absorb <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D(r)||)</marimo-tex> into a new radial coordinate</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">yielding the <strong>standard form</strong> (Eq. 24.6):</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nds^2 = -A(r)dt^2 + B(r)dr^2 + r^2(d\\theta^2 + \\sin^2\\theta\\,d\\phi^2).\n||]</marimo-tex></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "iLit",
      "code_hash": "464dd8d72e35a16d9bee13815c637d75",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"2-boundary-condition-from-asymptotic-flatness-eq-2415\">2) Boundary condition from asymptotic flatness (Eq. 24.15)</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The book imposes</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\n\\lim_{r\\to\\infty}A(r)=1,\\qquad \\lim_{r\\to\\infty}B(r)=1,\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">because far from the source spacetime should approach Minkowski space.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "TqIu",
      "code_hash": "7a988dc7d6d63918e7e1212717e77184",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"3-christoffel-symbols-used-in-the-derivation-eq-2417\">3) Christoffel symbols used in the derivation (Eq. 24.17)</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For the metric in Eq. (24.6), the non-zero Christoffels listed in the notes are:</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\n\\Gamma^r_{rr}=\\frac{B'}{2B},\\quad\n\\Gamma^r_{tt}=\\frac{A'}{2B},\\quad\n\\Gamma^r_{\\theta\\theta}=-\\frac{r}{B},\\quad\n\\Gamma^r_{\\phi\\phi}=-\\frac{r\\sin^2\\theta}{B},\n||]</marimo-tex><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\n\\Gamma^\\theta_{\\theta r}=\\Gamma^\\phi_{\\phi r}=\\frac{1}{r},\\quad\n\\Gamma^t_{tr}=\\frac{A'}{2A},\\quad\n\\Gamma^\\theta_{\\phi\\phi}=-\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta,\\quad\n\\Gamma^\\phi_{\\phi\\theta}=\\cot\\theta.\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">(Prime means <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(d/dr||)</marimo-tex>.)</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SFPL",
      "code_hash": "a5c1e045fcf847887a4078fd0b0ab22c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"4-ricci-components-in-the-notes-eq-2425\">4) Ricci components in the notes (Eq. 24.25)</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The reduced Ricci components are</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nR_{tt}=\\frac{A''}{2B}-\\frac{A'}{4B}\\left(\\frac{A'}{A}+\\frac{B'}{B}\\right)+\\frac{A'}{rB},\n||]</marimo-tex><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nR_{rr}=-\\frac{A''}{2A}+\\frac{A'}{4A}\\left(\\frac{A'}{A}+\\frac{B'}{B}\\right)+\\frac{B'}{rB},\n||]</marimo-tex><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nR_{\\theta\\theta}=1-\\frac{1}{B}-\\frac{r}{2B}\\left(\\frac{A'}{A}-\\frac{B'}{B}\\right).\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">In vacuum, set each to zero.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "BYtC",
      "code_hash": "d3eb84fc5101e5c7d0ff562b05d2753c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"5-key-linear-combination-eq-2426-2428\">5) Key linear combination (Eq. 24.26 -&gt; 24.28)</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The notes take</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nB R_{tt} + A R_{rr} = \\frac{1}{rB}(A'B+B'A)=0\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">so</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nA'B+B'A=0\n\\Rightarrow A(r)B(r)=\\text{const}.\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">Asymptotic flatness fixes the constant to 1, therefore</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nB(r)=\\frac{1}{A(r)}.\n||]</marimo-tex></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "cc29d41b7c6e4eca0a69f56f04a1c3c8",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"6-solve-with-r_thetatheta0-eq-2429-2430\">6) Solve with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(R_{\\theta\\theta}=0||)</marimo-tex> (Eq. 24.29 -&gt; 24.30)</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Substitute <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(B=1/A||)</marimo-tex> into <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(R_{\\theta\\theta}=0||)</marimo-tex>:</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nA-1+rA'=0\n\\iff (Ar)'=1.\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">Integrate:</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nAr=r+C\n\\Rightarrow A(r)=1+\\frac{C}{r}.\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">Then <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(R_{tt}=R_{rr}=0||)</marimo-tex> also hold.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Xref",
      "code_hash": "31b7e1554e1ef8e126a98dbae0e691e4",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"7-newtonian-matching-and-final-metric-eq-2431-2433\">7) Newtonian matching and final metric (Eq. 24.31, 24.33)</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The notes match to the weak-field limit</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nA(r)=-g_{00}\\approx 1+\\frac{2\\Phi}{c^2},\\qquad \\Phi=-\\frac{G_N M}{r},\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">giving</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nC=-\\frac{2G_NM}{c^2}.\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">So</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nds^2 = -\\left(1-\\frac{2G_NM}{c^2 r}\\right)c^2dt^2\n+\\left(1-\\frac{2G_NM}{c^2 r}\\right)^{-1}dr^2\n+r^2d\\Omega^2,\n||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">and with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(m=G_NM/c^2||)</marimo-tex> (Eq. 24.32):</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\nds^2=-f(r)dt^2+f(r)^{-1}dr^2+r^2d\\Omega^2,\n\\qquad f(r)=1-\\frac{2m}{r}.\n||]</marimo-tex></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
