          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"feedback\">Feedback</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Q1: Correct. That is exactly Eq. (24.26) -&gt; (24.27) plus asymptotic condition (24.15).</li>\n<li>Q2: Not quite. The step in the notes is (Ar)'=1 -&gt; Ar=r+C -&gt; A=1+C/r.</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "c26acc0f1ec1bdc149898db1967e7cb0",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"final-one-screen-summary-book-sequence\">Final one-screen summary (book sequence)</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Start with Eq. (24.1), simplify to Eq. (24.6).</li>\n<li>Compute Christoffels (Eq. 24.17).</li>\n<li>Use Ricci components (Eq. 24.25).</li>\n<li>Combine equations: Eq. (24.26) -&gt; <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(AB=\\mathrm{const}||)</marimo-tex> -&gt; Eq. (24.28).</li>\n<li>Use <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(R_{\\theta\\theta}=0||)</marimo-tex>: Eq. (24.29) -&gt; Eq. (24.30).</li>\n<li>Newtonian matching gives <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(C=-2G_NM/c^2||)</marimo-tex>.</li>\n<li>Arrive at Schwarzschild metric Eq. (24.31), or Eq. (24.33) with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(m=G_NM/c^2||)</marimo-tex>.</li>\n</ol>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This is exactly the derivation path in chapter 24.3.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
